In order to install "FormGet" used in the "Processing.nb" notebook,
you need to download FormRun-1.0.tar.gz from here:

https://feynarts.de/formcalc/

and unzip it. Then, from a Mathematica notebook, you need to run:

Needs["CCompilerDriver`"]
CreateExecutable[{"/Users/vb262523/Codes/FeynStuff/FormRun-1.0/FormGet.tm"}, "FormGet", "ShellOutputFunction" :> Print, "ShellCommandFunction" :> Print]

This command may give an error related to the fact that it does not
find MLCONST.  If this is the case, just replace:

typedef MLCONST char *cstring; --> typedef char *cstring;

in FormGet.tm inside the FormRun-1.0 folder. This should finally
produce the "FormGet" executable and CreateExecutable[...] should tell
you its location. Copy this exacutable in:

"/Applications/Mathematica.app/Contents/SystemFiles/Links/WSTP/DeveloperKit/MacOSX-x86-64/PrebuiltExamples".

Before running the "Processing.nb" notebook, you many need to adjust
the location of the "form" exactutable necessary to run
"FormGet[...]".

Finally, the resulting *.cc file will not immediately compile. Indeed,
it still require some manual editing to include some missing
declarations, and remove unused variables to suppress warnings.

